From: pmOS Mi8Lite <macosmojave2@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath10k: WCN3990/SDM660: encode scan channel list like qcacld

The WLAN.HL.1.0.1 firmware running in the SDM660 modem fatally asserts
(err_qdi.c EX:wlan_process) on the first channel tune of any scan,
active or passive, on any band. Verified on Xiaomi Mi 8 Lite (platina)
to be independent of: board data file used (all 18 device calibrations),
regdomain in the board data (0x809c and unlocked 0x0), firmware build
(c6-00023 and c6-00027), modem build (-00076 and -00087), regulators
(all rails verified on at runtime) and the RF reference clock (on).

What does differ is the WMI_SCAN_CHAN_LIST payload. qcacld (the stock
Android driver, which scans fine on the same device/firmware) sends per
channel only the regulatory power, in plain dBm, leaving max_power,
max_tx_power, antenna_max and reg_class_id at zero, and does not allow
VHT on 2.4GHz. Mainline ath10k sends max_power/reg_power/max_tx_power
as doubled half-dBm values (e.g. 40 for 20dBm) while the firmware's WMI
headers document max_tx_power as "1 dBm units"; the firmware's TPC
lookup against the per-device board data then fails at tune time.

Mirror the qcacld encoding on WCN3990.

Signed-off-by: pmOS Mi8Lite <macosmojave2@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -3449,7 +3449,11 @@
 			ch->allow_ht = true;
 
 			/* FIXME: when should we really allow VHT? */
-			ch->allow_vht = true;
+			if (QCA_REV_WCN3990(ar))
+				/* qcacld only allows VHT on 5GHz; mirror it */
+				ch->allow_vht = channel->band == NL80211_BAND_5GHZ;
+			else
+				ch->allow_vht = true;
 
 			ch->allow_ibss =
 				!(channel->flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_IR);
@@ -3481,9 +3485,26 @@
 			ch->freq = channel->center_freq;
 			ch->band_center_freq1 = channel->center_freq;
 			ch->min_power = 0;
-			ch->max_power = channel->max_power * 2;
-			ch->max_reg_power = channel->max_reg_power * 2;
-			ch->max_antenna_gain = channel->max_antenna_gain;
+			if (QCA_REV_WCN3990(ar)) {
+				/* The WLAN.HL.1.0.1 firmware on the SDM660
+				 * modem takes these fields the way qcacld
+				 * sends them: only the regulatory power, in
+				 * plain dBm (max_tx_power is documented as
+				 * "1 dBm units" in the WMI headers). The
+				 * doubled half-dBm values below make the TPC
+				 * lookup against the per-device board data
+				 * fail and the firmware fatally asserts on
+				 * the first channel tune of any scan
+				 * (err_qdi.c EX:wlan_process).
+				 */
+				ch->max_power = 0;
+				ch->max_reg_power = channel->max_reg_power;
+				ch->max_antenna_gain = 0;
+			} else {
+				ch->max_power = channel->max_power * 2;
+				ch->max_reg_power = channel->max_reg_power * 2;
+				ch->max_antenna_gain = channel->max_antenna_gain;
+			}
 			ch->reg_class_id = 0; /* FIXME */
 
 			/* FIXME: why use only legacy modes, why not any
